  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Major Performance & Memory Architecture Refactoring\n\n      - Replaced the worker-channel architecture with a Data-Oriented Design (DOD) pipeline, delivering up to 3x higher throughput under identical stress tests.\n      - Eliminated intermediate enqueue/dequeue worker channels and flush directly to the network stream, reducing latency and synchronization overhead.\n      - Introduced a contiguous append-and-flush buffer model, significantly improving cache locality and memory efficiency.\n      - Reduced memory usage by over 100x, maintaining approximately 100 MB RAM even under millions of continuous requests.\n      - Enhanced event-driven processing to fully leverage .NET ThreadPool efficiency without dedicated worker overhead.\n      - Minimized allocations and GC pressure across critical request-processing paths.\n\n      Benchmark Results\n\n      - Static Files: Over 140,000 requests/sec (~4 ms average latency).\n      - API Requests: Over 31,000 requests/sec.\n      - Up to 3x performance improvement compared to previous releases under the same benchmark conditions.",
